        "id": "ch8_1_5-1",
        "text": "File Inclusion\nFile inclusion can be exploited by pointing to a file path (locally or remotely) using\nthe URL. If the file is local on the web server, then we call it local file inclusion,\nFigure 8.26: Mutillidae \u2013 Command Injection\n218\nChapter 8 I Web Application Vulnerabilities\nand if the file is remote, then we call it remote file inclusion. This vulnerability\nis found in legacy applications developed in PHP and ASP when the developer\nforgets to validate the input to the function (you\u2019ll encounter this vulnerability\nin lots of CTF challenges).\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Local File Inclusion\n\u2022 Remote File Inclusion\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
